# Git — agent-controlled

The owner delegates **all Git work** to agents for `pageandportal/pageandportal`.

## Agents do

- `git init` / remotes / branches when needed for the website project
- Stage, commit, and push with clear messages (after substantive work or when the owner asks)
- Pull / merge / resolve simple conflicts when syncing with GitHub
- Keep binary assets in `supply/**/graphics/` and `supply/site/branding/` committed when supplied

## Agents do not

- Change `git config` (local or global)
- Force-push to `main` unless the owner explicitly requests it
- Commit `.env`, credentials, or secrets
- Skip hooks (`--no-verify`) unless the owner requests it
- Amend commits unless user rules allow (see commit skill)

## Remote

- **Origin:** https://github.com/pageandportal/pageandportal.git
- **Default branch:** `main`
- **Pages URL:** https://pageandportal.github.io/pageandportal/

## Commit style

One or two sentences focusing on **why**; note `version.properties` bumps when user-visible work ships.
